# Direct dependencies only. `requirements.txt` is generated from this file —
# do not edit it by hand.
#
#   uv pip compile backend/requirements.in -o backend/requirements.txt \
#       --python-version 3.13
#
# Why the split: requirements.txt used to be a pip freeze, so ~85 transitive
# packages were pinned alongside the ~30 real ones. Dependabot cannot tell the
# difference, so it bumped transitive pins independently of the parents that
# constrain them, and produced sets that cannot install. Three separate
# breakages in one day came from exactly that:
#
#   pydantic_core==2.47.0  vs  pydantic 2.13.4 requiring ==2.46.4
#   wrapt==2.3.0           vs  langfuse 4.0.0 requiring <2.0
#   tokenizers==0.23.1     vs  transformers 5.14.1 requiring <=0.23.0
#
# The last one merged and broke the production image build. Nothing named here
# is transitive, so there is no second pin left to drift out of range.

